WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:12.000
A query supplies a search value. A B-tree index keeps keys in order and uses a tree to find a key or key range.

00:12.000 --> 00:24.000
The matching index entry points to a table row. The query planner chooses whether to use the index. A small table can still use a table scan.

00:24.000 --> 00:38.000
An index takes storage space. A change to indexed data must also update the index. Evaluate read benefits and write costs with the actual workload.
